                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fca9a87e-ab88-30b4-b654-c26ea04e33e9",
                        "entry_id": "08f2a36b-a703-3da1-9924-6457face6b53",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The first part of the urogenital system to be differentiated in a vertebrate embryo, which functions as a simple excretory organ in simpler forms, serves as a provisional kidney in some fish and amphibians, and only appears as a temporary embryonic structure in reptiles, birds, and mammals."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c5cbb5e1-fe36-46f8-bba4-19d0108d1c40",
                                "sense_id": "fca9a87e-ab88-30b4-b654-c26ea04e33e9",
                                "text": "In addition, while in the pronephron only vacuolization was noted, the structure of the liver had an atypical appearance and there was a considerable number of erythrocytes scattered among the hepatic chords which themselves were noticeably altered."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "26bc6f9a-99df-4a84-95e3-47e3c5a9eed5",
                                "sense_id": "fca9a87e-ab88-30b4-b654-c26ea04e33e9",
                                "text": "The whole problem turned around a detailed understanding of the so-called Wolffian body, what modern textbooks in embryology designate as the pronephron and its associated Wolffian or pronephric ducts."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "716b79c9-f291-4ac4-b514-933d74b50d45",
                                "sense_id": "fca9a87e-ab88-30b4-b654-c26ea04e33e9",
                                "text": "Regression of the first clusters occurs before the total number of pronephron structures is established. The pronephrons induce the development of the mesonephrons. As the pronephrons regress, the mesonephrons appear."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
